   "design": "Class templates and instructor availability are kept in the booking system, which proposes the season schedule. The coordinator adjusts it there, instead of building it in a spreadsheet and typing it in. Instructor certificates sit in a register with expiry reminders. Members complete the health questionnaire and waiver online, stored with restricted access, so paper filing drops to exceptions. Monthly reports take their figures from a booking system query. Handling changes, answering mail, checking records and incident records stay with the coordinator.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Schedules, certificates and forms lived in spreadsheets and paper.",
   "enabler_now": "Booking systems with schedule templates, registers with reminders and online forms.",
   "still_hard": "Last-minute instructor absences.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which class members will not want moved.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less building and filing; people work stays.",
   "reach": [
